Negative control for filter-renderer.test.ts.

Stops the range control merging its write onto the column's current value, so
setting one end silently drops the other — the renderer deciding what the column
meant, which is what scoping the column rather than a leaf costs if the write is
not a merge. The assertion that reads the whole column after both ends are set
goes red; one that sets a single end, or reads the declaration rather than a
write, stays green.

